<title>FRANCE: Saint-Louis sells mushroom unit.</title>
<headline>Saint-Louis sells mushroom unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food group Saint-Louis said on Monday it agreed to sell its mushroom subsidiary Royal Champignon to the Champi-Jandou cooperative for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Royal Champignon produces and markets 80,000 tonnes of fresh and frozen mushrooms annually and generated sales of 965 million francs in 1995.</p>
<p>The sale is in line with Saint-Louis' strategy to focus on its core sugar and paper sector. The transaction must be approved by French authorities, Saint-Louis said in a statement.</p>
</text>
